# Reference for the generated `.env`. Template only — `.env` itself is git-ignored, and
# ./scripts/dev-up.sh and ./scripts/dev-start.sh rewrite it on every run. Editing `.env` by
# hand therefore has no effect past the next run.
#
#   LEHUB_SLOT   this workspace's slot. 0 is the main clone; each `git worktree` gets the
#                next free one. The database derives from it — see docs/local-dev.md.
#   LEHUB_SLUG   normalised name of the working tree directory.
#   LEHUB_DB     this workspace's database on the shared SQL Server instance.
#
# The ports derive from the slot too, a hundred apart, so slot 0 keeps exactly what the main
# clone always had:
#
#   LEHUB_API_PORT      7071, 7171, 7271, 7371
#   LEHUB_WEB_PORT      5173, 5273, 5373, 5473
#   LEHUB_ADMIN_PORT    5174, 5274, 5374, 5474
#   LEHUB_INSPECT_PORT  9229, 9329, 9429, 9529 — unused by default; pass it to
#                       `func start --inspect` to attach a debugger without clashing.
#
# MSSQL_SA_PASSWORD is a property of the *instance*, not of a workspace: SQL Server applies
# it only when it initialises an empty data directory, so every workspace has to present the
# same one. The single copy is generated once into the Git common directory — the one place
# every working tree shares and nothing versions — and reproduced here for
# docker-compose.yml and for running sqlcmd by hand. No working credential is committed,
# not even a local one.

LEHUB_SLOT=
LEHUB_SLUG=
LEHUB_DB=
LEHUB_API_PORT=
LEHUB_WEB_PORT=
LEHUB_ADMIN_PORT=
LEHUB_INSPECT_PORT=
MSSQL_SA_PASSWORD=
